epistle-panel for Debian
========================

This package does not install the panel. The panel runs only inside the
container image ghcr.io/glyndor/epistle-panel, as one service of the stack that
epistle generates. There is no standalone compose file.

What the package installs
-------------------------

  /usr/share/glyndor/epistle-panel/image    one line: ghcr.io/glyndor/epistle-panel:<version>
  /usr/share/glyndor/epistle-panel/README   what that file is for

The tag equals the package version, so `apt upgrade` is what moves the panel to
a new release. The reference has no digest because the digest is not known when
the package is built.

The package creates no account, no directory outside /usr/share and no secret.
epistle creates the panel's secrets and its API key next to its own data, and
the stack runs as epistle's account. `apt remove` and `apt purge` delete the two
files above and leave nothing behind.

Picking the panel up
--------------------

The design is that epistle reads the image file when it renders the stack. The
postinst of this
package has a hook for asking epistle to do that after an install or upgrade,
but it is empty: the epistle release that reads the file does not exist yet, and
the package does not guess at a command. Once epistle supports the panel, run

  sudo epistle stack update

to add or update the service. Until then installing this package changes
nothing in a running stack.
